# How to cite UbuKit: GitHub's "Cite this repository" reads this file, and so
# does Zenodo, which archives every GitHub Release and gives it a DOI. The
# version and date come from each release, so this file does not change with
# them.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use UbuKit, please cite the version you used, by its DOI on Zenodo.
type: software
title: UbuKit
abstract: >-
  Fuzzy, rough and classical clustering, self-organizing maps, evaluation
  metrics and TPE search, for Python and JavaScript.
authors:
  - family-names: Ubukata
    given-names: Seiki
repository-code: https://github.com/subukata/ubukit
# CFF reads several licenses as alternatives, so only UbuKit's own is listed;
# three small expressions in ARI and AMI follow scikit-learn under
# BSD-3-Clause (THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt).
license: MIT
keywords:
  - clustering
  - fuzzy c-means
  - rough clustering
  - self-organizing map
  - som-olp
  - tpe
